:: The Bunker Intro
<<set $outside to 0>>
You climb down a long, dirty ladder before entering some sort of bunker.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bunker]]>><<set $bunkerdepth to 0>><</link>>

:: Bunker
<<if $stress gte $stressmax and !$possessed>>
	<<passouttrash>>
<<else>>
	<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
	<<if $eventskip is 0>>
		<<rng>>
		<<if $rng gte 91>>
			<<eventbunkeritem>>
		<<elseif $danger gte (9900 - ($allure * $forestmod))>>
			<<eventbunker>>
		<<else>>
			<<eventbunkersafe>>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif $eventskip gte 1>>
		<<if $bunkerdepth lte 5>>
			You're in an abandoned bunker, the interior is dimly lit, and dust covers everything. As you glance over the walls of the bunker, you notice strange markings that seem to be in a language you've never seen before. The bunker seems to be in disrepair, and you wonder how long it's been since anyone has set foot here.
		<<else>>
			The deeper you go, the more deteriorated the the bunker becomes. There are pools of foul, stagnant water. Undoubtably the result of whatever leakage came from the landfill above.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<<if $bunkerdepth lt 10>>
			<<link [[Head deeper into the Bunker|Bunker]]>><<set $bunkerdepth += 1>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $bunkerdepth gt 0>>
			<<link [[Head back toward the exit|Bunker]]>><<set $bunkerdepth -= 1>><</link>>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<<if $bunkerdepth is 0>>
			<<link [[Exit the Bunker|Bunker Exit]]>><</link>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</if>>

<<set $eventskip to 0>>

:: Bunker Exit
<<set $outside to 1>>
You climb back up the dirty ladder before reaching the surface.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Trash]]>><</link>>